    This server attempts to implement the Minecraft server protocol for alpha
    version 1.0.15.  Pretty old!  Modern versions of Java have a little bit of
    trouble with this client, running the client with the following JVM option
    seems to get it working just fine.

      -Djava.util.Arrays.useLegacyMergeSort=true

    This file contains all my notes about the protocol as I assembled them. I
    am doing this entirely from a clean room as a learning process, I am not
    looking up the protocol on the internet as that would be too easy.

    Everything seems to use network byte order, big endian. Packets do not
    specify their lengths, so an unknown packet ID is irrecoverable which has
    downsides and benefits.


On Connect

    On connect, the client sends packet 0x01 followed by packet 0x0d, a full
    positional update. This position appears to be the same each time,
    containing the position for center of the central chunk.


Types

  byte

    Single byte.

  word

    Two bytes, big-endian order.

  dword

    Four bytes, big endian

  float

    Four byte floating point number, IEEE 754

  double

    Eight byte floating point number, IEEE 754

  bool

    Single byte, value is either 0 or 1

  string     length:word bytes:byte[length]

    Appears to be either an UTF-8 or ASCII string. First a word which is the
    byte length. Maximum of 65,535 bytes.


Client Packets

    These packets sent by the client to the server. There appears to be no
    packet length field, so unknown packets are irrecoverable for our server.

  Handshake Initiation (0x01) -- at least 11 bytes

    Sent by the client upon connection, appears to be the client identifying
    itself to the server.

      Fields

        type      value             notes
        dword(?)  unknown           0x0000000d
        string    username          (min 3, max 16 chars)
        string    password          defaults to 'Password'

      Example packet

        01
        00 00 00 0d
        00 07
        50 6c 61 79 65 72 33        "Player3"
        00 08
        50 61 73 73 77 6f 72 64     "Password"


  Player Grounded (0x0a)

    Indicates whether the player is standing/falling.

      Fields

        type      value             notes
        bool      grounded          true if grounded

      Example packet

        0a
        01

      Payload size

        1 byte

  Player Position (0x0b) -- 33 bytes

    Sent by the client when the player moves.

      Fields

        type      value             notes
        double    x-position
        double    y-position
        double    head y-position
        double    z-position
        bool      grounded          true if grounded

      Example packet

        0b
        40 1a 00 00 00 00 00 00
        40 50 32 fd b7 51 1b 96
        40 50 9a ab cb d1 1b 96
        40 88 74 00 00 00 00 00
        00


  Player Rotation (0x0c) -- 9 bytes

    Sent by the client when the player rotates around.

      Fields

        type      value             notes
        float     body rotation     in degrees
        float     head pitch        in degrees
        bool      grounded          true if grounded

      Example packet

        0c
        bf ac cc cd
        00 00 00 00
        01


  Player Full Position (0x0d) -- 41 bytes

    Combined 0x0a 0x0b 0x0c packet, full positional update.

      Fields

        type      value             notes
        double    x-position
        double    y-position
        double    head y-position
        double    z-position
        float     rotation
        float     head pitch
        bool      grounded          true if grounded

      Example packet

        0d
        40 21 00 00 00 00 00 00
        40 50 40 00 00 00 00 00
        40 50 a7 ae 14 80 00 00
        40 21 00 00 00 00 00 00
        c3 34 00 00
        00 00 00 00
        00


  Disconnect (0xff) -- at least 2 bytes

    Sent when the client disconnects.

      Fields

        type      value             notes
        string    reason            defaults to "Quitting"

      Example packet

        ff
        00 08
        51 75 69  74 74 69 6e 67    "Quitting"
